## What I built

**`src/cljc/dao/lease.cljc`** — new *The composition constructors* section (judge/holder/vocabulary untouched):

- **Medium declaration contract** (C2/C3): `check-medium-declaration!` validates `{:retention :evict-oldest|:complete, :capacity pos-int, :value-domain :portable-values|:host-values, :attribution …}` — declaration-based, never handle introspection. `:attribution` is one of D4's three source bindings (`:per-author-media`, `:envelope-key`, `:attachment-identity`), which is what makes resolver *compatibility* checkable: `check-resolver-compatibility!` requires `fn?` (presence) **and** `:resolver-bindings` covering every wired medium's declared kind — an incompatible resolver refuses exactly like a missing one.
- **`make-judge`**: requires `:cadence` (strictly positive, in-table, per-unit bound — the runtime/cadence declaration), non-empty `:ticks` and `:media`, resolver+bindings, `:reclaim`, `:writer`; delegates `:tolerance`/`:units`/`:drain-budget` validation to `initial-judge`; validates everything **before any wiring**. Returns `{:judge … :step judge-step :scope :process-scoped|:durable :cadence …}`.
- **`make-holder`**: requires `:tick` (the holder's own tick stream), `:fact` medium + declaration + resolver compatibility, plus `initial-holder`'s seams. Returns `{:holder … :tick … :fact … :scope …}`.
- **Durable gating** (C4): `:durable? true` requires `:durable-judge`, `:incarnation-rule`, `:fencing` (presence is all the vocabulary can check — adequacy is the resource's plan); non-durable returns `:scope :process-scoped`, so an unsettled composition cannot claim durable use.

**Test tree** — the reference tick driver (D3) lives in `test/dao/lease_test.cljc`: `tick-driver` is a **stepped, caller-driven deposit** (`deposit!`/`stop!`/`stopped?`/`appended`) with per-lane host clock policy under reader conditionals (clj `System/nanoTime`, cljs `js/Date.now`, cljd `DateTime.now` — the yin/repl.cljc idiom). No timer, callback, or sleep anywhere; C5 grep over `src/cljc/dao/lease.cljc` stays **zero**.

**`test/dao/lease_composition_test.cljc`** (new) — 8 deftests: `refusal-matrix-test`, `holder-refusal-matrix-test`, `process-scoped-fallback-test`, `end-to-end-grant-renew-lapse-test`, `non-ok-lapsed-append-leaves-lease-pending-test`, `forwarder-pause-sketch-test`, `served-connection-lifetime-sketch-test`, `shared-work-claim-sketch-test`.

## Per-invariant coverage

- **C1** — end-to-end drives the composed judge's own `:step`/`:judge` at declared `:cadence` over hand-turned ticks: grant → renewal → single `:silence` reclaim+record, no later re-record. Holder tick/fact wiring refused when absent.
- **C2** — matrix (23 cases + 11 holder cases): cadence missing/zero/foreign-unit, tick/media empty, entry wiring, declaration shape (retention/capacity/value-domain/attribution, incl. missing-retention), tolerance (delegated), resolver absent, bindings absent, **incompatible** resolver, writer, reclaim.
- **C3** — `:retention :neither` and retention-absent both refuse.
- **C4** — `:scope :process-scoped` on both constructors' non-durable values; durable with all three → `:scope :durable`; durable missing one/two/three → throws (per-seam key asserted).
- **C7** — end-to-end asserts the record survives the reclaimed resource; renewal-appending remains the control flow's own act (comment pin).
- **C8** — served-connection sketch (attachment-identity attribution): after lapse, `:lapsed` is on the grantor's writer and **never** on the holder's medium; the connection's closing is the resource event.
- **C5/C6** — grep zero over src; requires-only-dao.stream unchanged. Sketches are commented compositions (naming `serving/step!`, `close-session!`, `:ws/attachment`, `call-close!` as the real seams) with atom stand-ins — runnable wirings, not products.

